===Etymology===
From the variant {{m|it|ciriegia}}, from {{inh|it|VL.|ceresia}}, from the neuter plural of {{inh|it|LL.|ceresium}}, from {{inh|it|la|cerasium}}, from {{der|it|grc|κεράσιον||cherry}}, from {{m|grc|κερασός||[[bird cherry]]}}, ultimately possibly of {{der|it|ine-ana|-}} origin. Alternatively from {{m|it|ciliegio}}, {{m|it|ciriegio}} (Tuscan), from Late Latin {{m|la|ceresus}}, from Latin {{m|la|cerasus}}. See also {{m|it|cerasa}}.

Neither '''-li-''' or '''-gi'''  groups are the result of normal phonetical evolutions.  Lat. '''-ra-''' never evolves to Italian '''-Li''', nor '''sa'''→'''-gi'''<br>
The word is a hypercorrectism (like ''galera'') by Toscans afraid to pronounce the word as a Ligurian dialectalism. <br>

